# Olist E-Commerce Delivery Analysis\
\
## Project Overview\
This project analyzes Olist e-commerce order data using MySQL to understand delivery performance and identify patterns associated with late deliveries.\
\
## Business Questions\
- What percentage of delivered orders arrived late?\
- Which purchase months had the highest late-delivery rates?\
- Which product categories had higher late-delivery rates?\
\
## Tools Used\
- MySQL\
- SQL\
- CSV datasets\
\
## SQL Analysis\
The SQL queries examine:\
1. Overall late-delivery performance\
2. Monthly late-delivery trends\
3. Late-delivery rates by product category\
\
## Key Findings\
- **8.11%** of eligible delivered orders arrived later than the estimated delivery date.\
- March 2018 had the highest monthly late-delivery rate among the months analyzed, at **21.36%**.\
- The audio category had a late-delivery rate of **12.93%** among categories with at least 100 delivered orders.\
\
## Files\
- `olist_delivery_analysis.sql` \'97 SQL queries for delivery performance analysis.\
\
## Data Source\
Brazilian Olist e-commerce public dataset, originally published on Kaggle.\
\
## Notes\
Monthly and category-level rates are calculated from delivered orders with both actual and estimated delivery dates available. Product-category groups may overlap because an order can contain products from multiple categories.\
